    "description": "Natural Geode Specimen Lot - 7 Pieces\nQuartz Crystal Mineral Specimens\nRough Natural Formations\nThis collection features seven natural geode and crystal specimens displaying varied geological crystalline formations. Geodes form within hollow cavities of sedimentary or volcanic host rock through mineral-rich precipitation over geologic time. This lot showcases diverse textures, hollow vugs lined with sparkling quartz druse, and rugged weathered exterior rinds ideal for geological study, education, or natural specimen display.\nItems Included:\nLarge open geode half with prominent central cavity of quartz crystals\nOpen geode specimen displaying deep crystal-lined hollow pocket\nNatural crystalline cluster fragment with exposed quartz points\nRounded geode nodule with textured outer host rock matrix\nMiniature hollow geode with druzy crystal interior\nMatrix rock specimen section with exposed crystalline pocket\nGeode half featuring translucent to white quartz crystal cavity lining\nCondition:\nNatural geological specimens in rough, raw condition. All pieces retain their natural mineral surfaces, crystalline formations, and outer matrix without modern lapidary polishing. Natural earth dust, minor fracturing, and rough exterior edges inherent to raw mineral specimens.",
